{
 "_note": "TIER 1 as data: the declarative child tree \u2192 the flat DISPLAY LIST, its keyed DIFF, and its SVG serialisation. THE BUILD LAW: walk the children in document order; a wrapper (group \u00b7 blur \u00b7 shadow \u00b7 blend) emits NO op and instead folds into its descendants \u2014 transform composes (world = parentWorld \u00b7 local), opacity MULTIPLIES, paint attributes (fill \u00b7 stroke \u00b7 strokeWidth \u00b7 fillRule \u00b7 strokeLinecap \u00b7 strokeLinejoin) INHERIT, `clip` on a group rides every descendant op with the matrix in force where the clip was authored, and each effect wrapper APPENDS to the op's effect chain outermost-first. A `<gradient id>` child registers a paint and emits no op. Every shape becomes ONE op carrying its normalized path in LOCAL coordinates plus its world matrix \u2014 never a baked path, because tier 1 is retained and only the matrix changes when a transform animates. rect/circle/ellipse become paths through the SAME arc\u2192cubic converter as `d`, so a circle is four cubics with k = 4/3\u00b7tan(\u03c0/8) on every renderer. THE UNSTYLED DEFAULT IS SVG's \u2014 black fill, no stroke, strokeWidth 1, nonzero \u2014 because the vocabulary is SVG's. THE KEY LAW (the `<list>` keying law verbatim): an authored `key` wins, an unkeyed node keys on its KIND plus its position among same-kind siblings, a duplicate gets the `\u00b7n` suffix in encounter order, and the key is PATH-PREFIXED by its ancestors' keys. THE DIFF LAW: keys present on both sides KEEP their identity across reorder; the move set is the complement of a longest increasing subsequence of the retained previous indices, so a single item moved to the front is ONE move, not n. An unknown child tag is one diagnostic and no op \u2014 a canvas draws, it does not lay out. `svg` is the SSR serialisation of the same display list, byte-pinned: the tier-1 tree renders server-side as SVG and hydrates onto a canvas with no repaint flash.",
